<html><title>Unknown Listings</title>
<h1>Unknown</h1>

<i>Unknown</i>, which also went by the titles <i>Unknown Fantasy Fiction</i>
(Feb 1940 - Aug 1941), and <i>Unknown Worlds</i> (Oct 1941 -Oct 1943), was
the fantasy companion to <i>Astounding</i>. It was edited by John W. Campbell, Jr.
for its entire print run (1939-1943).
<p>
Despite it's short life, <i>Unknown</i> was highly praised, even though a 
later attempt in 1948 to revive the magazine failed. The later
<i>Galaxy</i> fantasy companion, <i>Beyond Fantasy Fiction</i> was
an imitator of the magazine; a number of anthologies gleaned from
<i>Unknown</i> were published: <i>The Unknown</i>, <i>The Unknown Five</i>,
and <i>Hell Hath Fury</i>.
